group=group-0</panel_attributes><additional_attributes></additional_attributes></element><element><id>UMLNote</id><coordinates><x>0</x><y>0</y><w>328</w><h>480</h></coordinates><panel_attributes>CSIT121 - Assignment 1

Your task is to analyze, design, and implement PetMatch, 
a pet breed information management system,
using information available from Purina Australia.

PetMatch will &lt;store&gt; &lt;pet breed&gt; profiles so that &lt;users&gt; can maintain 
and explore information about different breeds. 

Model the domain using classes, attributes, methods, 
object relationships. 

Purina Australia provides breed information for &lt;cats&gt; and &lt;dogs&gt;.
Its breed pages describe characteristics such as size, coat, energy level,
color, weight, temperament, shedding, and activities. 
You do not need to reproduce every field or every breed. 

Use OOA to identify the key entities needed by PetMatch, 
define appropriate attributes and behaviors, 
establish meaningful relationships among the classes. 
The four required system operations are add, search, edit, and delete.

1. OOA:
Design a system that includes at least three classes,
each with attributes and behaviors relevant to pet breed
information management. 

2. OOD: 
Create a UML class diagram to illustrate your 
class design and relationships. 

3. OOP: 
Implement the system in Python using OOP principles such as
association, composition, and aggregation where appropriate. 

4. Unit test: 
Test the system by writing at least one unit test in Python to
verify a core functionality (e.g., searching for a pet using breed name).
